{"book":24,"chapter":28,"context":{"chapter":28,"title":"Hananiah's Broken Yoke","summary":"In the temple the prophet Hananiah announces that within two years God will break Babylon's yoke, and he snaps the wooden yoke on Jeremiah's neck. Jeremiah answers that God has made a yoke of iron instead, and Hananiah dies within months.","background":"The scene is dated to Zedekiah's fourth year, about 594 BC. Jeremiah applies the test of Deuteronomy 18:21-22: a prophet whose word does not come to pass has not spoken for the Lord. Hananiah dies in the seventh month (v. 17), just two months after his prophecy in the fifth (v. 1).","customs":[{"term":"Yokes of wood… yokes of iron","verses":"28:13","note":"A wooden yoke can be snapped; an iron one cannot. Resisting God's discipline only makes it heavier."}],"watchFor":["Jeremiah's 'Amen: the Lord do so' (v. 6): he wishes Hananiah were right.","'Thou hast taught rebellion against the Lord' (v. 16) echoes Deuteronomy 13:5.","Compare the dates in vv. 1 and 17."],"connections":["Deuteronomy 18:21-22","Deuteronomy 13:5","Jeremiah 27:2","Ezekiel 13:6"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיְהִי","vayhi","H1961","Hc/Vqw3ms","and it was"],["בַּשָּׁנָה","bashanah","H8141","HRd/Ncfsa","in the year"],["הַהִיא","hahi'","H1931","HTd/Pp3fs","<the> that"],["בְּרֵאשִׁית","bereshit","H7225","HR/Ncfsc","in [the] beginning of"],["מַמְלֶכֶת","mamlekhet","H4467","HNcfsc","[the] reign of"],["צִדְקִיָּה","tzidkiyah","H6667","HNpm","Zedekiah"],["מֶלֶךְ","melekh-","H4428","HNcmsc","[the] king of"],["יְהוּדָה","yehudah","H3063","HNpl","Judah"],["בַּשָּׁנָה","bishnat","H8141","HRd/Ncfsa","in the year"],["הָרְבִעִית","harevi'it","H7243","HTd/Aofsa","<the> fourth"],["בַּחֹדֶשׁ","bachodesh","H2320","HRd/Ncmsa","in the month"],["הַחֲמִישִׁי","hachamishi","H2549","HTd/Aomsa","<the> fifth"],["אָמַר","'amar","H559","HVqp3ms","he said"],["אֵלַי","'elai","H413","HRd/Sp1bs","to me"],["חֲנַנְיָה","chananyah","H2608","HNpm","Hananiah"],["בֶן","ven-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son